Krita Nova 73 - Transform tool: Ctrl + drag a corner moves it freely

In Free Transform, holding Ctrl and dragging one of the frame's corner
handles moves that corner freely (distort), as in Photoshop: the
transform, unchanged so far, goes over to the Perspective (4 points) mode,
whose corners move freely, and the drag goes on there. The bar's mode icon
and the tool options follow. Ctrl + drag anywhere else does what it did
(the 3D perspective of Krita's free transform). Not for vector layers,
which cannot take a perspective.

